evidence_source:
In modbus_reply():
  offset = ctx->backend->header_length;
  slave = req[offset - 1];
  function = req[offset];
  address = (req[offset + 1] << 8) + req[offset + 2];
No prior check that req_length >= offset+3.

In modbus_reply(), case MODBUS_FC_WRITE_MULTIPLE_REGISTERS:
  int nb = (req[offset + 3] << 8) + req[offset + 4];
  int nb_bytes = req[offset + 5];
  ... only checks: nb < 1 || nb > MAX || nb_bytes != nb*2
  ...
  for (i = mapping_address, j = 6; i < mapping_address + nb; i++, j += 2) {
      mb_mapping->tab_registers[i] = (req[offset + j] << 8) + req[offset + j + 1];
  }
No check that req_length >= offset + 6 + 2*nb before indexing.

In modbus_reply(), case MODBUS_FC_WRITE_AND_READ_REGISTERS:
  int nb_write = (req[offset + 7] << 8) + req[offset + 8];
  int nb_write_bytes = req[offset + 9];
  ... only checks: nb_write < 1 || nb_write > MAX || nb < 1 || nb > MAX || nb_write_bytes != nb_write*2
  ...
  for (i = mapping_address_write, j = 10; i < mapping_address_write + nb_write; i++, j += 2) {
      mb_mapping->tab_registers[i] = (req[offset + j] << 8) + req[offset + j + 1];
  }
No verification that req_length >= offset + 10 + 2*nb_write.
